  "stem": "The brightness \\(I(d)\\), in lux, of a lamp measured at a distance of \\(d\\) meters from the lamp is given by \\(I(d) = \\frac{72}{d^{2}}\\). What is the brightness, in lux, measured 3 meters from the lamp?",
  "figure": null,
  "answer_type": "spr",
  "choices": null,
  "answer": null,
  "spr_answers": [
    "8"
  ],
  "solution": [
    "Substitute \\(3\\) for \\(d\\): \\(I(3) = \\frac{72}{3^{2}} = \\frac{72}{9}\\).",
    "\\(\\frac{72}{9} = 8\\) lux."
  ],
  "explanation": null,
  "traps": null,
  "verify": "d = symbols('d')\nI = Lambda(d, 72/d**2)\nassert I(3) == 8\nassert [Rational(s) for s in spr_answers] == [8]",
